    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45913" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐχέ-φρων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρήν</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sensible, prudent</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ ἀγαθὸς καὶ ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.341
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				13.332
			</span></i>; freq. as epith. of Penelope, <i><span class="en">
				4.111
			</span></i>, etc.; later of animals, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύλακες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					16.226
				</span></i>
			: late in Prose, Syn.Alch.<i><span class="en">
				p.65
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νως</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				15.33
			</span></i>.</div>
